{"kind":"report","text":"Verdict: APPROVED. J4's live witness closes the done-when rows of parent 0c3091fa as stated, with the limits below. Checker review for request ac656693. This verdict deploys nothing, and it is not S1 completion.\n\nI read the sealed unit's public results directly and didn't rely on the report's table. The unit reruns clean: `SHA256SUMS` digest fdbcf91d, 162 files, none writable. Receipts show exit 0, capture 0, complete and no timeout for setup and all six later phases. The state chain holds from 292e2636 through a17ae935, ad15c8bd, 571e0b16, 731bcfe4 and fb1b8082 to 89e929d1, and each later phase's parent equals the previous state. Setup's stderr holds only the DEP0205 warning, which answers the one log you didn't reread.\n\n## The rows\n\n**Two agents push to their own hold's forks: closed.** In `work`'s `gitResponses`, fork 23-24-1 takes receive-pack 200 for commit 880b6007, and fork 28-29-1 takes it for 402f376c. Each token's push to the other fork and to the room answers 403 at discovery, with no POST. Each credential answered 403 to the wrong key, 200 to the owner and 403 to a repeat.\n\n\"Agents\" here means two members of kind and role agent whose keys one operator script used. No hosted agent engine ran. That is enough for this row, because the row tests the adapter's fork and credential scoping, and it does not show an agent running on its own. The hosted agent witness stays owed.\n\n**A token stops working when its hold ends: closed, by token 5.** The row says \"a token\", and one token on the real provider meets it. Token 5's receive-pack discovery answered 200 at 23:00:53.631, the release is lane seq 37, the revoke outcome is seq 38, and the same route with the same token answered 403 at 23:00:58.276, with 14 min 50 s left on its stated end. So expiry can't explain it. The two controls hold: the independent token read the fork with 200 before and after, and token 6 wrote at 23:00:58.673, so the provider hadn't stopped writing in general.\n\nThe evidence doesn't reach these, and you state each one:\n- Token 6 has native records only.\n- A hold that ends by time has no provider read. Holds 9 and 16 show native revokes only.\n- The probe is a write, so a read with a revoked token wasn't tried.\n- It shows that the token stopped, and it doesn't show why.\n\n**The change publishes from the chosen fork: closed.** The manifest at seq 46 names 402f376c and tree 2a0159cc, the commit that hold 28's fork took. The review is seq 47, the merge is seq 48 with state `published`, publication 10 binds that manifest and commit, and written receipt 13 names the commit. A provider read of the room's branch returns the commit. No fresh clone compared the bytes, as you say. The commit ID binds the tree, so I accept this for the row. S1's third room did compare bytes on another room.\n\n**On the deployment: closed, within the attestation.** Worker version da13242c is in the results. Its link to source 112eff12 stays the operator's attestation, as it has throughout.\n\n## What this doesn't cover\n\n- I ran no control, rehearsal or live read, and no second independent read covers this verdict.\n- The parent's \"not before\" order wasn't rechecked. That was the planner's sequencing, and it doesn't change what the witness observed.\n- This is one run on one provider result set, and `ownerMayReview:true` is the scratch policy.\n- The independent token's read scope rests on the planner's attestation. Its revocation has a denied read before expiry, in `channel/revoked-git-read/channel-result.json`.\n- The unmeasured items stay unmeasured, as you list them: the Membership window, write latency and the slow-Worker case at head. The two S1 summary 403s stay unexplained, and Register stays unobserved.\n- A scan of the unit for token shapes found only the `Bearer` literal in `packet-source-v16/git.mjs`, which is source code.\n\n## Leftovers\n\nThe planner holds these, as `cleanup`'s result names them: four forks whose provider state nobody has read, two forks' refs, and the room read token until 00:00:51 UTC. The workspace tokens read ended, and the independent token is revoked.\n\n## For the planner\n\nYou may deploy main as far as this witness is concerned. A deployment voids V13's remaining use, which no longer matters, since every phase has run. The deployment carries S4, S5, S6, the finding item, hosted loop reads, omitted lanes, S1 and the finding views. Hold further deployments during the real room's run, as S1's runbook says.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: the adapter does what plan 029 asked, on the real provider, for one run.\n- Security: scoping held at every probe in this run. No secret is in the public unit, by that scan.\n- Simplification: the operator and its evidence were costly for a scratch witness, and the sprint report's cost review already says so.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f0cebb5328ce889422a3bf097023a4e6ce93c76d stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:01e0dd696d953e8a4209c9e0a7461afc19c30b9a, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:043d587ef18b62fdeee6b57f8968de1567206697, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:070231aadcb17348891458bc2eedb5bbf529860c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:171f5f57d26458ff1e85c1f9e0a69fefb342bc9b and 19 more"}}